{"messages":[{"createdAt":"2026-11-27T05:39:24.2143042\u002B00:00","role":"assistant","contents":[{"$type":"reasoning","text":"I\u0027m working out the Program.cs for their agent from the page\u0027s listing, since the guide itself doesn\u0027t include that file. I\u0027m weighing whether to add a settings block, and I\u0027m noting that the page\u0027s configuration lives in .env files.\n\nThe settings for the agent go in .env files, with ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and LLM_PROFILE as the two named values. The program loads the coding demo\u0027s catalogue, so for an agent of their own I\u0027d note they need to swap in their own catalogue. Usage is one-shot, passing a prompt on the command line.\n\nI\u0027m settling on the reply\u0027s closing line: the CLI project doc, src/docs/projects/LouisAgent.Cli.md, since that\u0027s where CliHost is named.\n\nI\u0027m working out the closing part of the reply: the settings block and how the catalogue fits in. The catalogue is what makes the agent its own, so I\u0027ll note that CodingCatalog.Create() would need swapping for a catalogue of their own, and that the build-your-own guides cover identities and packs.\n\nI\u0027m settling on the offer at the end: a build-your-own identity first, then a pack, then walking through a line of Program.cs if they want.\n\n","protectedData":"CAQS0h8KEAgUGAI4AUIIdGhpbmtpbmcSDNCCBNCWWcUelXWNixoMhqaXS69mdMD\u002B/cVOIjC4QDVVExYzhMeds595hhkuND2auUJ7DR/OjOlJ31ex\u002BEfTQCZpLocxPUmofkaE3xAq7x4\u002BCeVxoTIcgyJXWA065/A\u002BCZ8kOSeNM8tqwnx8ARXCM47wi0Rd\u002BIfz7vMaJgf7j7vXEi86GHwB1rYzQXBrmrfxgkT2ZhtOxO2lYRY2GsyVQR3KgM5WZrgiIsjr3xvb3FACdS9V942pPPnjKfNblWrq/m4WW8r/8zrPZyUW/vwN\u002BrfmoMCekvijUwL\u002BIUCN84t5PZHRl1iSdEAK3hTe8i161ZD7cUWsFp0sVyNqbT2OV0OJEXRq5m67RZ1xEJVjBqchm4PkCr8rtv0CA\u002BZyxJdQ\u002BArArx8YlbLSPfAFUJeCsnGFyh\u002Buzqebd5x\u002B1Vts/uu/MSWKomBsbWrsRC8YSw6rtqXOE7zzB3QUOY7lsnZFMJ0vS5uNzRwMmG6kPyEFooHO6VNZPVWIV8b62COPeG7uzQq4ZSH/ZOlHwdrpE5nvbfdBjgnPycws08UdeWEJ6dPDnvfjRY5EKgPjFShZc8aUnW6M